     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. This would be about twice the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe intended dose may have been one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.** These are common regimens.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you've verified it. I'd still advise checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
